WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.541
Hi, I'm Ines!

00:00:02.541 --> 00:00:05.864
Let me show you how a whole team of agents can be

00:00:05.864 --> 00:00:07.802
scaled by looping them like one transformer.

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:11.662
Not a bigger model, not more agents.

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:12.936
Scale the collaboration itself.

00:00:12.936 --> 00:00:16.121
Loop the team in latent space and let it refine.

00:00:18.192 --> 00:00:20.410
The usual way, agents talk in text.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.579
Every hand-off decodes to words and then reads them back.

00:00:23.999 --> 00:00:28.047
This system keeps the hidden states instead, and trains the whole team as one.

00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:33.418
Three agents become the layers of one network.

00:00:33.418 --> 00:00:35.869
Here a planner, a solver, and a critic.

00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:40.093
Inside each agent an inner link turns its last hidden state

00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:41.477
into its next input.

00:00:41.477 --> 00:00:43.552
Latent thoughts, never written as words.

00:00:43.972 --> 00:00:47.612
An outer link carries those latent states to the next agent, even

00:00:47.612 --> 00:00:49.433
when the models have different sizes.

00:00:49.853 --> 00:00:52.403
The last agent loops back to the first.

00:00:52.403 --> 00:00:56.865
Round after round the team refines, and only the final round decodes to text.

00:00:58.442 --> 00:01:00.110
The link itself is tiny.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:04.115
A residual carries the embedding through, and a two-layer network learns only

00:01:04.115 --> 00:01:05.783
the gap between the spaces.

00:01:06.203 --> 00:01:08.173
A residual carries the embedding through.

00:01:09.249 --> 00:01:11.125
A two-layer net learns only the gap.

00:01:13.342 --> 00:01:15.283
Deeper recursion cuts more tokens.

00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:19.941
About thirty-five percent at one round, up to seventy-six at three, because

00:01:19.941 --> 00:01:22.271
the middle steps are never re-decoded.

00:01:23.592 --> 00:01:29.023
13.12M trainable parameters, 0.31% of the weights.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.950
So the whole team trains as one.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:36.693
Agents as layers, latent links instead of text, and recursion as a

00:01:36.693 --> 00:01:37.941
new axis to scale.

00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:40.539
Agents become layers.

00:01:40.539 --> 00:01:41.948
Latent links, not text.

00:01:41.948 --> 00:01:44.061
Loop for more, at lower cost.

00:01:44.481 --> 00:01:46.545
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:46.545 --> 00:01:47.135
I'm Ines.

00:01:47.135 --> 00:01:47.430
Bye!
